module bindings.java.locale_resource_path_validation;

// Locale-driven resource selection joins the locale's subtags into the
// resource path with underscores -- the localized-resource naming
// convention documented on java.util.Locale and ResourceBundle
// (base_language_country_variant.ext). Hand-rolled joiners concatenate
// Locale.getLanguage()/getCountry()/getVariant() straight into the path
// they resolve, and a request-derived locale (Accept-Language via
// ServletRequest.getLocale) lets subtags carry '/' and '..' into the
// joined path, escaping the resource root once the path reaches
// ServletContext.getResource, a ClassLoader resource lookup or a URL.
// The documented safe forms keep the subtag validation in the joining
// code: a syntax check on the subtag values (String.matches against
// the Locale JavaDoc grammar) or a locale-parsing API that rejects
// malformed tags (Locale.forLanguageTag, Locale.Builder setters).
// ResourceBundle.getBundle applies the fallback chain itself and never
// lets the caller build the path.
//
// The judgement lives in the pack rule; this binding only recognises
// the shape. The getter clauses read binary-expression tokens, which
// the AST produces only for real concatenations -- prose in a comment
// satisfies neither side, and a getter compared or assigned rather
// than joined emits no such token. The validation clause is an
// exact-token call match, so a subtag check in a sibling method does
// not clear the join.

binding localeSubtagResourcePathWithoutValidation {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function"
    and containsAny(node.context.expr, ["getLanguage()", "getCountry()", "getVariant()"])
    and containsAny(node.context.expr, ["+'_'+", "+\"_\"+"])
    and not (node.context.call in ["matches", "forLanguageTag", "setLanguage", "setLanguageTag"])
  emit issue code.UnvalidatedLocaleFileInclude at node
}
